.TH YACE 1 "2026-11-09" "yace" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
yace \- a fast, light, terminal-native multi-root code editor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B yace
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIPATH\fR]
.br
.B yace
\fIFILE\fR[:\fILINE\fR[:\fICOLUMN\fR]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B yace
is a code editor for the terminal with VS Code's keys and concepts:
multi-root workspaces (it reads VS Code and Cursor
.I .code-workspace
files), a file Explorer, fuzzy Quick Open (\fBCtrl+P\fR), the Command
Palette (\fBCtrl+Shift+P\fR), workspace search and replace, an integrated
terminal, language servers, Git, tree-sitter highlighting, themes and
native plugins.
.PP
\fIPATH\fR decides what opens:
.TP
.I a folder
opens it as the workspace.
.TP
.I a file
opens just that file, with no folder (like \fBcode file.js\fR).
\fIFILE:LINE:COLUMN\fR opens it at that position.
.TP
.I a .code-workspace file
opens the multi-root workspace it describes.
.TP
.I nothing
reopens the most recent workspace (or an empty window).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-workspace " " \fIFILE\fR
Open this \fI.code-workspace\fR file.
.TP
.BR \-\-add\-root " " \fIDIR\fR
Add another folder to the workspace (repeatable).
.TP
.BR \-\-goto " " \fIFILE\fR[:\fILINE\fR[:\fICOL\fR]]
Open a file at a position (together with a folder or workspace).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-restore
Do not restore the previous session (tabs, layout) for this workspace.
.TP
.BR \-\-safe\-mode ", " \-\-no\-plugins
Start without loading any plugin code or plugin grammars.
.TP
.BR \-\-install\-plugin " " \fIPATH\fR
Install a plugin from a folder or a \fI.tar.gz\fR package, then exit.
Asks for confirmation unless \fB\-\-yes\fR is given.
.TP
.B \-\-list\-plugins
List installed plugins, then exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-package\-plugin " " \fIDIR\fR " [" \-o " " \fIFILE\fR]
Validate a plugin folder and build a \fI.tar.gz\fR package, then exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/yace/config.toml
User settings (TOML). Also \fIkeybindings.toml\fR, \fIthemes/\fR and
\fIplugins/\fR in the same folder.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/yace/
Sessions, recent workspaces and, with \fBYACE_LOG\fR, the log file.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/yace/
Caches (the Quick Open index when \fBsearch.cacheIndex\fR is on).
.PP
Workspace folders may hold \fI.vscode/settings.json\fR, which YACE reads.
Removing the package never touches these files.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.BR YACE_CONFIG_DIR ", " YACE_STATE_DIR ", " YACE_CACHE_DIR
Use these folders instead of the defaults above.
.TP
.B YACE_LOG
Write a log (\fBYACE_LOG=debug\fR, \fBinfo\fR…) to the state folder. Off by
default; file contents are never logged.
.TP
.B YACE_OPENER
The program "Reveal in File Manager" runs (default \fBxdg\-open\fR).
.TP
.B YACE_MALLOC_TRIM=0
Do not return freed memory to the system after large jobs.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
yace .                        open the current folder
yace ~/Dev/api                open a folder
yace file.js                  open just that file
yace src/main.rs:42:8         a file at line 42, column 8
yace ~/work.code-workspace    a multi-root workspace
yace api \-\-add\-root ../web    two unrelated folders together
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
Documentation: https://abedmurrar.github.io/yace/
.br
Source and issues: https://github.com/abedmurrar/yace
